cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "link" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'link: Intrinsic Habitat Potential and Fish Passage Connectivity for Stream
  Networks'
version: 0.65.0
abstract: 'Models where fish habitat could be on a stream network and whether fish
  can reach it. For each species it classifies stream reaches, lakes and wetlands
  as spawning or rearing habitat from rules on gradient, channel size and waterbody
  type. It resolves which reaches each species can reach past falls and steep gradients,
  using fish observations and habitat confirmations as evidence of passage, and marks
  each of those reaches with the kind of human-made barrier below it, if any: a road
  or rail crossing, or a dam. Every rule and threshold is a row in a config bundle,
  and every run records its inputs, so a result traces back to the rule that produced
  it. Runs on the British Columbia Freshwater Atlas through ''fresh''. Experimental:
  APIs and outputs change without notice.'
